message: "If you use this software or data, please cite them using these metadata."
title: "LPFid: test oracles for the fidelity of Linux livepatch modules"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kazuru
    given-names: Seke
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-4099-1059"
    email: kazuruuni@gmail.com
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/kazuru-chidumbwe/lpfid"
# identifiers:
#   - type: doi
#     value: 10.5281/zenodo.TBD
#     description: Zenodo version of record (filled after first GitHub release)
abstract: >-
  Blind reference-differential binding oracle for Linux livepatch modules (frozen
  versions through v1.6, including rules RF and RS), the fault operators that edit
  built modules, the selection and build scripts for a corpus of 150 CVE fixes on
  stable kernels, the loader, presence-test and generator-comparison runners, and
  every run record behind the reported results.
keywords:
  - livepatch
  - test oracle
  - mutation analysis
  - Linux kernel
